    ^{:line 115} sync/Mutex


    ^{:line 118 :tag uint32 :doc "Base register\n"} Base

    ^{:line 120 :tag uint32 :doc "Clock gate register\n"} CCGR

    ^{:line 122 :tag int :doc "Clock gate\n"} CG

    ^{:line 124 :tag int :doc "Interrupt ID\n"} IRQ










    ^{:line 135 :tag (* dma/Region) :doc "DeriveKeyMemory represents the DMA memory region used for exchanging DCP\nderived keys when the derivation index points to an internal DCP key RAM\nslot. The memory region must be initialized before DeriveKey().\n\nIt is recommended to use a DMA region within the internal RAM (e.g.\ni.MX6 On-Chip OCRAM/iRAM) to avoid exposure to external RAM.\n\nThe DeriveKey() function uses DeriveKeyMemory only if the default\nDMA region start does not overlap with it.\n"} DeriveKeyMemory


